      "data": {
        "text": "**Constructing The Project**\n\nOkay, I'm currently focused on structuring this multi-file Python project. I need to create nine new files for key management and encryption, keeping `encrypt_payload.py` as is. For each \"SAME-SCENARIO\" and \"LATER-STEP\" file, an external provider is necessary. Right now, I'm working to make the \"HELPER\" functions reusable.\n\n\n**Analyzing The Approach**\n\nI've been analyzing the structure of `encrypt_payload.py` to understand its current KMS usage. I'm solidifying plans for provider integrations, specifically focusing on AWS KMS for key management and encryption. I'm also planning to utilize AWS CloudWatch Logs for logging and auditing and AWS Comprehend for content moderation. I'm outlining how each new file will interact with these providers, and establishing how the HELPER functions will be reusable. I am focusing on the key management aspect first.\n\n\n**Defining Project Files**\n\nI am now focusing on defining the new files required for this project, and I've broken down the project goals. I'll be leaving the initial `encrypt_payload.py` unchanged and will focus on creating the remaining files. I've decided to establish provider integrations using `boto3` for AWS services, including KMS for key management, Comprehend for content moderation, Translate for translation, and CloudWatch Logs for logging and auditing. I've created plans for `security_client.py` for client creation, and `security_models.py` for supporting data structures. I will be working on creating the `decrypt_payload.py` and `envelope_encrypt.py` files next.\n\n\n**Outlining Provider Usage**\n\nI'm now reading the existing `encrypt_payload.py` to understand its KMS usage, allowing me to plan the structure. I've chosen AWS KMS for key management, Comprehend for content moderation, Translate for translation, and CloudWatch Logs for logging. Next, I will be defining `security_client.py` using `boto3` and the supporting `security_models.py` files. I am working on how the KMS, Comprehend, Translate, and CloudWatch Logs integrations will work.\n\n\n",
