        "text": "**Adapting to KMS**\n\nI've hit a slight snag, I need to adapt the plan. It seems `encrypt_payload.py` is tied to Google Cloud KMS and not AWS KMS. This means the key management strategy for the \"SAME-SCENARIO\" files needs a Google Cloud KMS focus now.\n\n\n**Refining KMS Strategy**\n\nI've decided to refine the KMS strategy. Since `encrypt_payload.py` utilizes Google Cloud KMS, I'll stick with Google Cloud for all Key Management Service operations. This extends to `decrypt_payload.py` and `envelope_encrypt.py` as well. For the \"LATER-STEP\" files, I will use Google Cloud services like Google Cloud Logging, Google Cloud DLP, and Google Cloud Translation. This approach ensures consistency within the Google Cloud ecosystem.\n\n\n**Finalizing Google Cloud Strategy**\n\nNow I have a comprehensive Google Cloud strategy. I've cemented Google Cloud KMS for all key management, including `decrypt_payload.py`, `envelope_encrypt.py`, and `sign_or_verify_key.py`. Furthermore, I'll leverage Google Cloud Logging, Cloud DLP, and Cloud Translation for the \"LATER-STEP\" files to maintain platform consistency. I have also decided on the precise order of implementation for the files. I'm now starting by creating `security_models.py`.\n\n\n",
